{"task_id": "Mbpp/62", "solution": "def smallest_num(input_list: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the smallest number in a list of numerical values.\n    Assumes the input list is not empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_value = input_list[0]\n    for num in input_list:\n        if num < min_value:\n            min_value = num\n    return min_value"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/63", "solution": "def max_difference(tuple_list: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum absolute difference between elements within pairs\n    in a given list of numerical tuples. Returns 0 if the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not tuple_list:\n        return 0\n\n    max_diff = 0\n    for element1, element2 in tuple_list:\n        current_diff = abs(element1 - element2)\n        if current_diff > max_diff:\n            max_diff = current_diff\n\n    return max_diff"}
