{"task_id": "Mbpp/82", "solution": "def volume_sphere(radius: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the volume of a sphere given its radius. Raises ValueError if the radius is negative.\"\"\"\n    import math\n\n    class Sphere:\n        \"\"\"Represents a sphere. Provides methods for calculating its volume.\"\"\"\n\n        def __init__(self, radius: float):\n            \"\"\"Initializes a Sphere object with a given radius. Raises ValueError if the radius is negative.\"\"\"\n            if radius < 0:\n                raise ValueError(\"Radius cannot be negative.\")\n            self._radius = radius\n\n        def calculate_volume(self) -> float:\n            \"\"\"Calculates the volume of the sphere. Returns the calculated volume.\"\"\"\n            return (4/3) * math.pi * (self._radius ** 3)\n\n    sphere_obj = Sphere(radius)\n    return sphere_obj.calculate_volume()"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence using memoization.\n    P(1) = 1, P(2) = 1, P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n - P(n-1)) for n > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    _sequence_cache = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\n    def _calculate(k: int) -> int:\n        if k in _sequence_cache:\n            return _sequence_cache[k]\n\n        p_k_minus_1 = _calculate(k - 1)\n        term1 = _calculate(p_k_minus_1)\n        term2 = _calculate(k - p_k_minus_1)\n\n        _sequence_cache[k] = term1 + term2\n        return _sequence_cache[k]\n\n    return _calculate(n)"}
