{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "def common_in_nested_lists(nested_lists: list[list]) -> set:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds elements common to all sub-lists within a given nested list.\n    Returns an empty set if the input list is empty or no common elements are found.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_lists:\n        return set()\n\n    # Initialize common_set with elements from the first sub-list\n    common_set = set(nested_lists[0])\n\n    # Iterate through the rest of the sub-lists\n    for sub_list in nested_lists[1:]:\n        current_set = set(sub_list)\n        common_set = common_set.intersection(current_set)\n        # If common_set becomes empty, no more common elements are possible\n        if not common_set:\n            break\n\n    return common_set"}
