{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "def pancake_sort(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of comparable elements in ascending order using the pancake sort algorithm.\n    It creates a mutable copy to avoid modifying the original list.\n    \"\"\"\n    arr = list(input_list)\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    for curr_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find the index of the maximum element in the current sublist (0 to curr_size-1)\n        max_idx = arr.index(max(arr[:curr_size]))\n\n        if max_idx != curr_size - 1:\n            # Move the maximum element to the beginning by flipping the prefix up to max_idx\n            arr[:max_idx+1] = arr[:max_idx+1][::-1]\n\n            # Move the maximum element to its correct position by flipping the entire current sublist\n            arr[:curr_size] = arr[:curr_size][::-1]\n\n    return arr"}
