{"task_id": "Mbpp/170", "solution": "def sum_range_list(numbers: list[int], start_index: int, end_index: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of numbers in a list within a specified inclusive range.\n    Raises ValueError if inputs violate business rules (BR1-BR6).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        raise ValueError(\"The list 'numbers' cannot be empty.\")\n    if not (0 <= start_index < len(numbers)):\n        raise ValueError(f\"start_index ({start_index}) is out of bounds for list of length {len(numbers)}.\")\n    if not (0 <= end_index < len(numbers)):\n        raise ValueError(f\"end_index ({end_index}) is out of bounds for list of length {len(numbers)}.\")\n    if start_index > end_index:\n        raise ValueError(f\"start_index ({start_index}) cannot be greater than end_index ({end_index}).\")\n\n    return sum(numbers[start_index : end_index + 1])"}
