{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence in the given array.\n    A bitonic subsequence is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Calculate LIS sums ending at each position\n    lis_sums = [arr[i] for i in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lis_sums[i] = max(lis_sums[i], lis_sums[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Calculate LDS sums starting at each position (traverse from right to left)\n    lds_sums = [arr[i] for i in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lds_sums[i] = max(lds_sums[i], lds_sums[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Combine LIS and LDS sums to find the maximum bitonic subsequence sum\n    # Subtract arr[i] once because it's included in both LIS and LDS sums\n    max_bitonic_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, lis_sums[i] + lds_sums[i] - arr[i])\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
