{"task_id": "Mbpp/290", "solution": "def max_length(list_of_lists: list) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sub-list with the maximum length in a list of lists.\n    Returns (0, None) if the input list_of_lists is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        return 0, None\n\n    max_len = 0\n    max_list = None\n\n    for sub_list in list_of_lists:\n        current_length = len(sub_list)\n        if current_length > max_len:\n            max_len = current_length\n            max_list = sub_list\n\n    return (max_len, max_list)"}
