{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "def large_product(list1, list2, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the specified number of largest products from two given lists.\n    One factor is selected from each list.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    class Number:\n        def __init__(self, value: float):\n            self.value = float(value)\n\n    class Product:\n        def __init__(self, factor1: Number, factor2: Number):\n            self.factor1 = factor1\n            self.factor2 = factor2\n            self.value = self.factor1.value * self.factor2.value\n\n        def get_value(self) -> float:\n            return self.value\n\n    class LargestProductsFinder:\n        @staticmethod\n        def find_largest_products(list1_raw: list, list2_raw: list, k: int) -> list:\n            all_products = []\n            for num1_val in list1_raw:\n                for num2_val in list2_raw:\n                    num_obj1 = Number(num1_val)\n                    num_obj2 = Number(num2_val)\n                    product_obj = Product(num_obj1, num_obj2)\n                    all_products.append(product_obj.get_value())\n\n            # Sort all products in descending order and take the top k\n            all_products.sort(reverse=True)\n            return all_products[:k]\n\n    return LargestProductsFinder.find_largest_products(list1, list2, k)"}
