{"task_id": "Mbpp/391", "solution": "def convert_list_dictionary(list1: list, list2: list, list3: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts three input lists into a list of nested dictionaries.\n    Each element at a corresponding index across the three lists forms a single\n    nested dictionary entry: {'list1_element': {'list2_element': list3_element}}.\n    \"\"\"\n    output_list = []\n    for i in range(len(list1)):\n        outer_key = list1[i]\n        inner_key = list2[i]\n        inner_value = list3[i]\n        output_list.append({outer_key: {inner_key: inner_value}})\n    return output_list"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "_memo = {}\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum for n using the recursive formula\n    f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n), with memoization.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    if n <= 1:\n        _memo[n] = n\n        return n\n\n    # Integer division for all fractional components\n    sum_parts = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5)\n    )\n\n    result = max(sum_parts, n)\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
