{"task_id": "Mbpp/409", "solution": "def min_product_tuple(input_list: list[tuple[int | float, int | float]]) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"Finds the minimum product from a list of tuples.\n\n    Calculates the product of each pair and returns the smallest product.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _validate_input(input_list: list[tuple[int | float, int | float]]) -> None:\n        # Per strict requirements, this validation function is a no-op, assuming valid input types.\n        pass\n\n    def _calculate_tuple_product(tup: tuple[int | float, int | float]) -> int | float:\n        # Calculates the product of two numerical elements in a tuple.\n        return tup[0] * tup[1]\n\n    def _find_minimum_product(products: list[int | float]) -> int | float:\n        # Determines the minimum value from a list of products.\n        return min(products)\n\n    _validate_input(input_list)\n\n    products = []\n    for tup in input_list:\n        products.append(_calculate_tuple_product(tup))\n\n    return _find_minimum_product(products)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/410", "solution": "def min_val(input_list: list) -> (int | float | None):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum numerical value within a given heterogeneous list,\n    ignoring non-numerical elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_value = None\n    for item in input_list:\n        if isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n            if min_value is None or item < min_value:\n                min_value = item\n    return min_value"}
