{"task_id": "Mbpp/418", "solution": "def Find_Max(input_list: list[list]) -> list | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the element (inner list) of a list having maximum length.\n    If multiple inner lists have the same maximum length, the first one encountered is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return None\n\n    max_element = None\n    max_length = -1\n\n    for inner_list in input_list:\n        current_length = len(inner_list)\n        if current_length > max_length:\n            max_length = current_length\n            max_element = inner_list\n\n    return max_element"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(arr: list) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds a pair with the highest product from a given array of integers.\n    Returns an empty tuple () if the input array has fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(arr) < 2:\n        return ()\n\n    arr.sort()\n\n    # The maximum product can be either from the two largest numbers\n    # or from the two smallest (most negative) numbers.\n    product_of_largest = arr[-1] * arr[-2]\n    product_of_smallest = arr[0] * arr[1]\n\n    if product_of_largest > product_of_smallest:\n        return (arr[-2], arr[-1])\n    else:\n        return (arr[0], arr[1])"}
