{"task_id": "Mbpp/457", "solution": "def Find_Min(list_of_lists: list[list]) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sublist with the minimum length from a collection of lists.\n\n    Args:\n        list_of_lists: A list of lists (e.g., [[1],[1,2],[1,2,3]]).\\n\n    Returns:\n        The sublist with the minimum length. If multiple sublists share\n        the same minimum length, any one of them can be returned.\n        Returns None if the input list_of_lists is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        return None\n\n    min_length_sublist = None\n    min_length = float('inf')\n\n    for sublist in list_of_lists:\n        current_length = len(sublist)\n        if current_length < min_length:\n            min_length = current_length\n            min_length_sublist = sublist\n\n    return min_length_sublist"}
