{"task_id": "Mbpp/458", "solution": "class Rectangle:\n    \"\"\"Represents a rectangle with length and width, and calculates its area.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, length: float, width: float) -> None:\n        if not isinstance(length, (int, float)) or not isinstance(width, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"Length and width must be numerical.\")\n        if length < 0 or width < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Length and width must be non-negative.\")\n\n        self._length = float(length)\n        self._width = float(width)\n\n    @property\n    def length(self) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Getter for the rectangle's length.\"\"\"\n        return self._length\n\n    @property\n    def width(self) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Getter for the rectangle's width.\"\"\"\n        return self._width\n\n    def calculate_area(self) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Calculates and returns the area of the rectangle.\"\"\"\n        return self._length * self._width\ndef rectangle_area(length: float, width: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the area of a rectangle given its length and width.\n    It handles type and value validation internally.\n    \"\"\"\n    rectangle = Rectangle(length, width)\n    return rectangle.calculate_area()"}
