{"task_id": "Mbpp/598", "solution": "def armstrong_number(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given number is an Armstrong number.\n    An Armstrong number is equal to the sum of its own digits, each raised to the power of the number of digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return False\n    if number == 0:\n        return True\n\n    original_number = number\n    num_digits = 0\n    digits = []\n    temp_num = number\n\n    # Extract digits and count the number of digits\n    while temp_num > 0:\n        digits.append(temp_num % 10)\n        temp_num //= 10\n        num_digits += 1\n\n    # Calculate the sum of each digit raised to the power of the total number of digits\n    calculated_sum = 0\n    for digit in digits:\n        calculated_sum += digit ** num_digits\n\n    return calculated_sum == original_number"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/605", "solution": "def prime_num(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the given integer is a prime number.\"\"\"\n    if number <= 1:\n        return False\n    if number == 2:\n        return True\n    if number % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n    \n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= number:\n        if number % i == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 2\n    return True"}
