{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "def get_ludic(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates and returns all ludic numbers less than or equal to n using a sieve process.\n    It starts with natural numbers, removing elements based on the next found ludic number.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        return []\n\n    # Initialize a list of candidate numbers from 1 to n.\n    candidates = list(range(1, n + 1))\n    ludic_numbers = []\n\n    # Continue the sieve process as long as there are candidates.\n    while candidates:\n        # The first number in the candidates list is the next ludic number.\n        ludic_num = candidates.pop(0)\n        ludic_numbers.append(ludic_num)\n\n        # For ludic_num > 1, remove every ludic_num-th element from the remaining candidates.\n        if ludic_num > 1:\n            next_candidates = []\n            count = 0\n            for candidate in candidates:\n                count += 1\n                if count % ludic_num != 0:\n                    next_candidates.append(candidate)\n            candidates = next_candidates\n            \n    return ludic_numbers"}
