{"task_id": "Mbpp/610", "solution": "def remove_kth_element(input_list: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a new list with the k'th (1-based) element removed from input_list.\n    If k is out of bounds, a copy of the original list is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    length = len(input_list)\n    # Convert 1-based index k to 0-based index\n    idx = k - 1\n\n    # Check if the 0-based index is out of bounds\n    if idx < 0 or idx >= length:\n        return input_list[:]  # Return a shallow copy of the original list\n\n    # Construct the new list by concatenating slices\n    # The part before the element to be removed\n    first_part = input_list[:idx]\n    # The part after the element to be removed\n    second_part = input_list[idx + 1:]\n\n    return first_part + second_part"}
