{"task_id": "Mbpp/619", "solution": "def _is_digit(char: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Determines if a given character is a digit ('0'-'9').\"\"\"\n    return '0' <= char <= '9'\ndef _separate_characters(input_string: str) -> tuple[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"Separates the input string into non-digit and digit parts, preserving relative order.\"\"\"\n    non_digits = []\n    digits = []\n    for char in input_string:\n        if _is_digit(char):\n            digits.append(char)\n        else:\n            non_digits.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(non_digits), \"\".join(digits)\ndef _concatenate_parts(non_digits: str, digits: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Combines the non-digit string and the digit string into a single output string.\"\"\"\n    return non_digits + digits\ndef move_num(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Moves all numeric characters to the end of the given string.\n    Preserves the relative order of non-numeric characters and numeric characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    non_digits_str, digits_str = _separate_characters(input_string)\n    return _concatenate_parts(non_digits_str, digits_str)"}
