{"task_id": "Mbpp/632", "solution": "def move_zero(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Moves all zeroes to the end of the list while preserving the relative order of non-zero elements.\n    Returns the reordered list.\n    \"\"\"\n    non_zeroes = []\n    zeroes = []\n    for element in input_list:\n        if element == 0:\n            zeroes.append(element)\n        else:\n            non_zeroes.append(element)\n    non_zeroes.extend(zeroes)\n    return non_zeroes"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "def get_coordinates(coordinate_tuple: tuple[int, int]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts all adjacent coordinates of the given coordinate tuple, forming a 3x3 grid.\n    Includes the central coordinate itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    x, y = coordinate_tuple\n    adjacent_coords = []\n    for dx in range(-1, 2):  # -1, 0, 1\n        for dy in range(-1, 2):  # -1, 0, 1\n            new_x = x + dx\n            new_y = y + dy\n            adjacent_coords.append([new_x, new_y])\n    return adjacent_coords"}
