{"task_id": "Mbpp/644", "solution": "def reverse_Array_Upto_K(arr: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses the order of elements in the input array from index 0 up to k-1 (inclusive).\n    Raises ValueError if k is negative or k exceeds the length of the array.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k < 0 or k > len(arr):\n        raise ValueError(\"k must be a non-negative integer and not exceed the array's length.\")\n\n    start = 0\n    end = k - 1\n    while start < end:\n        arr[start], arr[end] = arr[end], arr[start]\n        start += 1\n        end -= 1\n    return arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/725", "solution": "def extract_quotation(input_string: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts all substrings enclosed by double quotation marks from an input string.\n    Returns a list of extracted values, excluding the quotation marks.\n    \"\"\"\n    extracted_values = []\n    in_quote = False\n    current_value = []\n\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char == '\"':\n            if in_quote:\n                # End of a quoted section\n                extracted_values.append(\"\".join(current_value))\n                current_value = []\n                in_quote = False\n            else:\n                # Start of a quoted section\n                in_quote = True\n        elif in_quote:\n            # Append character to the current value if inside quotes\n            current_value.append(char)\n\n    return extracted_values"}
